WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Nosebleeds are very common and, in most cases, they are not serious.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.000
Our main goals are simply to stop the bleeding and make sure the person doesn't swallow any blood.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.500
To start, have the person sit down and lean forward.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.500
Be sure they do not tilt their head back, as that can cause blood to run down their throat.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.500
Next, you'll want to firmly pinch the soft lower part of the nose right at the nostrils

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.500
and hold that continuous pressure for at least 10 to 15 minutes.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
It's important not to release the pressure to check on it too early,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.500
and you should avoid packing the nose with cotton or tissues.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.500
If the bleeding doesn't stop after that initial pressure,

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.500
you can try applying an ice pack to the bridge of the nose while continuing to pinch the nostrils.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:48.500
While we can usually handle these ourselves, you should seek medical care if you think the nose might be broken.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.500
Go ahead and call 911 if the bleeding hasn't stopped after 15 minutes,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.500
or if the person is having trouble breathing.

